1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,870
More than one hundred men,

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,700
women and children...

3
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:06,009
vanished. No graves.

4
00:00:06,009 --> 00:00:07,504
No sign of a fight.

5
00:00:07,504 --> 00:00:08,344
Just one word,

6
00:00:08,344 --> 00:00:10,133
carved into a wooden post.

7
00:00:10,133 --> 00:00:11,973
More than four hundred years later,

8
00:00:11,973 --> 00:00:14,819
it's still one of America's greatest mysteries.

9
00:00:14,819 --> 00:00:16,240
So what really happened?

10
00:00:20,067 --> 00:00:21,750
August 1590

11
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:24,230
An English ship drops anchor off the coast of

12
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:25,475
North America

13
00:00:25,475 --> 00:00:25,475
On board is a man who has waited three

14
00:00:27,655 --> 00:00:30,080
long years to get back to his daughter...

15
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:31,963
and his baby granddaughter

16
00:00:31,963 --> 00:00:31,963
His name is John White

17
00:00:33,777 --> 00:00:36,377
He's the governor of a tiny English colony

18
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:36,400
But when he reaches the settlement,

19
00:00:38,140 --> 00:00:39,391
it's empty

20
00:00:39,391 --> 00:00:41,426
More than one hundred people...

21
00:00:41,426 --> 00:00:42,360
gone

22
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:42,360
The only clue?

23
00:00:43,895 --> 00:00:44,654
A single word,

24
00:00:44,654 --> 00:00:46,464
carved into a wooden post

25
00:00:46,464 --> 00:00:46,464
More than four hundred years later,

26
00:00:48,404 --> 00:00:50,687
we still don't know what it means

27
00:00:50,437 --> 00:00:50,687
This is the mystery of the Lost Colony of

28
00:00:53,027 --> 00:00:54,147
Roanoke

29
00:00:57,767 --> 00:00:59,167
To understand this mystery,

30
00:00:59,167 --> 00:01:01,367
we need to go back to the 1580s,

31
00:01:01,367 --> 00:01:03,727
when England was racing Spain to build an

32
00:01:03,727 --> 00:01:05,807
empire in the Americas

33
00:01:05,551 --> 00:01:05,821
Spain had already grown rich from gold and

34
00:01:08,241 --> 00:01:10,158
silver in the New World

35
00:01:09,888 --> 00:01:10,158
So Queen Elizabeth gave an explorer named Sir

36
00:01:12,778 --> 00:01:15,378
Walter Raleigh permission to start a colony

37
00:01:15,549 --> 00:01:15,820
A year earlier,

38
00:01:16,799 --> 00:01:19,119
his explorers had come home with stories of a

39
00:01:19,119 --> 00:01:19,519
rich,

40
00:01:19,519 --> 00:01:20,360
green land,

41
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:21,699
and two local men,

42
00:01:21,699 --> 00:01:23,459
Manteo and Wanchese

43
00:01:23,337 --> 00:01:23,607
In 1585,

44
00:01:24,947 --> 00:01:27,227
his first group of men landed on Roanoke

45
00:01:27,227 --> 00:01:27,587
Island,

46
00:01:27,587 --> 00:01:29,920
in what's now North Carolina

47
00:01:29,650 --> 00:01:29,920
John White came too,

48
00:01:31,180 --> 00:01:32,020
as an artist,

49
00:01:32,020 --> 00:01:33,060
painting the people,

50
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:35,332
plants and animals he saw

51
00:01:35,062 --> 00:01:35,332
But things went wrong fast

52
00:01:37,187 --> 00:01:38,427
They ran short of food,

53
00:01:38,427 --> 00:01:40,859
and quarreled with the local people

54
00:01:40,589 --> 00:01:40,859
Fighting broke out,

55
00:01:41,919 --> 00:01:43,959
and trust between the English and some of their

56
00:01:43,959 --> 00:01:45,719
neighbors was shattered

57
00:01:45,479 --> 00:01:45,749
But one man,

58
00:01:46,662 --> 00:01:47,009
Manteo,

59
00:01:47,009 --> 00:01:48,409
from Croatoan island,

60
00:01:48,409 --> 00:01:51,009
stayed a loyal friend to the English

61
00:01:50,805 --> 00:01:51,075
After less than a year,

62
00:01:52,334 --> 00:01:54,402
the men gave up and sailed home

63
00:01:54,402 --> 00:01:56,476
But Raleigh wasn't done

64
00:01:56,056 --> 00:01:56,476
Next time,

65
00:01:57,256 --> 00:01:59,336
he would send families

66
00:02:03,067 --> 00:02:04,047
In 1587,

67
00:02:04,047 --> 00:02:05,772
a new group set sail

68
00:02:05,772 --> 00:02:06,412
And this time,

69
00:02:06,412 --> 00:02:08,367
it wasn't just soldiers

70
00:02:08,097 --> 00:02:08,367
There were farmers,

71
00:02:09,347 --> 00:02:09,987
craftsmen,

72
00:02:09,987 --> 00:02:11,027
and whole families,

73
00:02:11,027 --> 00:02:13,627
including women who were expecting babies

74
00:02:13,825 --> 00:02:14,095
About one hundred and fifteen men,

75
00:02:16,155 --> 00:02:17,315
women and children,

76
00:02:17,315 --> 00:02:19,439
coming to build a real town

77
00:02:19,169 --> 00:02:19,439
Each family was promised a large piece of land

78
00:02:22,059 --> 00:02:23,500
in the New World

79
00:02:23,230 --> 00:02:23,500
Their leader was John White,

80
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:27,200
the artist who had painted the land and its

81
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:29,023
people on the first trip

82
00:02:28,753 --> 00:02:29,023
Manteo sailed with them,

83
00:02:30,563 --> 00:02:33,071
coming home after a trip to England

84
00:02:32,801 --> 00:02:33,071
But here's the thing:

85
00:02:34,131 --> 00:02:36,713
they were never supposed to settle on Roanoke

86
00:02:36,713 --> 00:02:38,113
The plan was further north,

87
00:02:38,113 --> 00:02:39,873
near Chesapeake Bay

88
00:02:39,817 --> 00:02:40,087
On the way,

89
00:02:40,707 --> 00:02:42,067
they stopped at Roanoke,

90
00:02:42,067 --> 00:02:44,107
just to check on a few men left there

91
00:02:44,107 --> 00:02:45,584
the year before

92
00:02:45,314 --> 00:02:45,584
And then the ship's captain refused to take

93
00:02:48,044 --> 00:02:49,135
them any further

94
00:02:49,135 --> 00:02:50,975
He left them on Roanoke Island,

95
00:02:50,975 --> 00:02:52,814
late in the summer

96
00:02:52,394 --> 00:02:52,814
And what they found was a bad sign

97
00:02:54,885 --> 00:02:56,325
The old fort was torn down,

98
00:02:56,325 --> 00:02:58,925
and the empty houses were overgrown with weeds

99
00:03:03,667 --> 00:03:04,707
On August 18th,

100
00:03:04,707 --> 00:03:06,827
John White's daughter Eleanor gave birth to a

101
00:03:06,827 --> 00:03:08,111
baby girl

102
00:03:07,841 --> 00:03:08,111
Her husband,

103
00:03:08,891 --> 00:03:09,891
Ananias Dare,

104
00:03:09,891 --> 00:03:11,756
was one of the colonists

105
00:03:11,486 --> 00:03:11,756
They named her Virginia

106
00:03:13,604 --> 00:03:15,764
She was the first English child born in the

107
00:03:15,764 --> 00:03:16,884
Americas

108
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:17,070
Days later,

109
00:03:17,890 --> 00:03:20,427
another baby was born in the colony

110
00:03:20,157 --> 00:03:20,427
But the colony was already in trouble

111
00:03:22,759 --> 00:03:24,319
It was too late in the year to plant

112
00:03:24,319 --> 00:03:25,395
crops

113
00:03:25,125 --> 00:03:25,395
The supplies they'd brought from England were

114
00:03:27,335 --> 00:03:28,658
running low

115
00:03:28,388 --> 00:03:28,658
And relations with some of the local people

116
00:03:30,758 --> 00:03:31,988
were tense

117
00:03:31,718 --> 00:03:31,988
Manteo was baptized as a Christian,

118
00:03:34,208 --> 00:03:36,808
and named Lord of Roanoke by the English

119
00:03:36,991 --> 00:03:37,261
So the colonists asked John White to sail back

120
00:03:39,761 --> 00:03:40,441
to England,

121
00:03:40,441 --> 00:03:42,196
and bring help

122
00:03:41,776 --> 00:03:42,196
White was their governor,

123
00:03:43,456 --> 00:03:44,961
and leaving felt wrong

124
00:03:44,961 --> 00:03:47,041
But the colonists insisted

125
00:03:51,067 --> 00:03:52,655
Think about that choice

126
00:03:52,655 --> 00:03:55,255
White didn't want to leave his family behind

127
00:03:55,315 --> 00:03:55,585
His daughter...

128
00:03:57,084 --> 00:03:59,684
and a granddaughter only nine days old

129
00:03:59,701 --> 00:03:59,971
So before he left,

130
00:04:01,111 --> 00:04:03,384
they agreed on a simple signal

131
00:04:03,114 --> 00:04:03,384
The colonists were already planning to move

132
00:04:05,644 --> 00:04:07,724
about fifty miles inland

133
00:04:07,522 --> 00:04:07,792
If they moved,

134
00:04:08,612 --> 00:04:10,412
they would carve the name of the place they'd

135
00:04:10,412 --> 00:04:10,772
gone,

136
00:04:10,772 --> 00:04:12,894
on a tree or a post

137
00:04:12,624 --> 00:04:12,894
That way,

138
00:04:13,614 --> 00:04:16,205
anyone coming back would know where to look

139
00:04:15,935 --> 00:04:16,205
And if they were in danger,

140
00:04:17,585 --> 00:04:20,065
they would carve a cross above it

141
00:04:19,795 --> 00:04:20,065
A cross would mean:

142
00:04:21,045 --> 00:04:21,885
come quickly,

143
00:04:21,885 --> 00:04:23,473
we need help

144
00:04:23,203 --> 00:04:23,473
White promised to be back within months

145
00:04:25,826 --> 00:04:26,706
He sailed away,

146
00:04:26,706 --> 00:04:29,306
leaving his daughter and granddaughter behind

147
00:04:29,328 --> 00:04:29,748
He had no idea it would be the last

148
00:04:31,728 --> 00:04:34,128
time he ever saw them

149
00:04:37,567 --> 00:04:39,007
But when White reached England,

150
00:04:39,007 --> 00:04:41,541
the country was preparing for war

151
00:04:41,271 --> 00:04:41,541
Spain's King Philip had built a giant fleet to

152
00:04:43,961 --> 00:04:45,401
conquer England

153
00:04:45,230 --> 00:04:45,500
A huge Spanish fleet,

154
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:47,520
the Armada,

155
00:04:47,520 --> 00:04:49,484
was coming to invade

156
00:04:49,214 --> 00:04:49,484
In the summer of 1588,

157
00:04:51,384 --> 00:04:53,664
English ships fought the Armada in the English

158
00:04:53,664 --> 00:04:54,659
Channel

159
00:04:54,389 --> 00:04:54,659
The Queen needed every ship she had

160
00:04:57,056 --> 00:04:59,482
None could be spared for the colony

161
00:04:59,212 --> 00:04:59,482
White begged for help

162
00:05:01,119 --> 00:05:03,439
But a few colonists far across the ocean

163
00:05:03,439 --> 00:05:05,719
weren't the Queen's first concern

164
00:05:05,449 --> 00:05:05,719
He did find two small ships,

165
00:05:07,379 --> 00:05:09,459
but they were attacked at sea and forced to

166
00:05:09,459 --> 00:05:10,685
turn back

167
00:05:10,415 --> 00:05:10,685
French pirates robbed them of almost

168
00:05:12,705 --> 00:05:13,825
everything

169
00:05:13,612 --> 00:05:13,882
Months turned into years

170
00:05:15,770 --> 00:05:17,730
It would be three whole years before he saw

171
00:05:17,730 --> 00:05:19,170
Roanoke again

172
00:05:18,942 --> 00:05:19,362
Finally,

173
00:05:19,942 --> 00:05:21,022
in 1590,

174
00:05:21,022 --> 00:05:23,142
he found a place on ships sailing out to

175
00:05:23,142 --> 00:05:25,222
hunt for Spanish treasure

176
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:29,740
On August 18th,

177
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:30,740
1590,

178
00:05:30,740 --> 00:05:32,950
White finally landed on Roanoke

179
00:05:32,950 --> 00:05:35,550
It was his granddaughter's third birthday

180
00:05:35,326 --> 00:05:35,596
From the ship,

181
00:05:36,336 --> 00:05:38,574
they saw smoke rising on the island

182
00:05:38,574 --> 00:05:40,619
Was it the colonists?

183
00:05:40,349 --> 00:05:40,619
As they came closer,

184
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:44,649
his men blew a trumpet and sang English songs

185
00:05:44,649 --> 00:05:46,089
Nobody answered

186
00:05:46,123 --> 00:05:46,393
They waited near the shore through the night

187
00:05:48,601 --> 00:05:49,041
At dawn,

188
00:05:49,041 --> 00:05:50,903
they walked to the village

189
00:05:50,633 --> 00:05:50,903
The houses had been taken down,

190
00:05:52,563 --> 00:05:55,163
and a tall wooden fence stood around the site

191
00:05:55,359 --> 00:05:55,629
Heavy things,

192
00:05:56,369 --> 00:05:57,889
like iron bars and lead,

193
00:05:57,889 --> 00:05:59,009
had been left behind,

194
00:05:59,009 --> 00:06:00,960
now buried in grass

195
00:06:00,690 --> 00:06:00,960
There were no graves

196
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:04,475
And no sign of a battle

197
00:06:04,205 --> 00:06:04,475
White found his own chests,

198
00:06:06,175 --> 00:06:07,988
dug up and broken open

199
00:06:07,988 --> 00:06:08,588
His books,

200
00:06:08,588 --> 00:06:11,188
maps and pictures were ruined by the rain

201
00:06:11,267 --> 00:06:11,537
Everyone was gone

202
00:06:13,116 --> 00:06:13,686
More than one hundred people had simply...

203
00:06:16,429 --> 00:06:17,549
disappeared

204
00:06:21,733 --> 00:06:23,200
And then they found it

205
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:24,600
On a post of the fence,

206
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:26,374
someone had carved a single word:

207
00:06:26,374 --> 00:06:27,494
CROATOAN

208
00:06:27,773 --> 00:06:28,043
The bark had been stripped away,

209
00:06:29,503 --> 00:06:31,183
and the letters were cut neatly,

210
00:06:31,183 --> 00:06:32,943
in large capitals

211
00:06:32,799 --> 00:06:33,069
On a nearby tree were three more letters:

212
00:06:35,689 --> 00:06:35,849
C,

213
00:06:35,849 --> 00:06:36,129
R,

214
00:06:36,129 --> 00:06:37,127
O

215
00:06:36,857 --> 00:06:37,127
These were the signs the colonists had promised

216
00:06:39,547 --> 00:06:40,647
to leave

217
00:06:40,377 --> 00:06:40,647
And there was no cross

218
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:44,077
No sign of danger

219
00:06:43,807 --> 00:06:44,077
It looked as if they had left calmly

220
00:06:46,261 --> 00:06:47,701
In peace

221
00:06:47,442 --> 00:06:47,712
Croatoan was the name of an island about fifty

222
00:06:50,612 --> 00:06:51,412
miles south,

223
00:06:51,412 --> 00:06:53,379
home to friendly people

224
00:06:53,109 --> 00:06:53,379
It was also the home of Manteo,

225
00:06:55,158 --> 00:06:57,238
the colonists' loyal friend

226
00:06:57,148 --> 00:06:57,418
White was sure his family had gone there

227
00:06:59,684 --> 00:07:00,004
Help,

228
00:07:00,524 --> 00:07:01,004
it seemed,

229
00:07:01,004 --> 00:07:03,604
was just one short voyage away

230
00:07:07,367 --> 00:07:09,618
So why didn't White just go and get them?

231
00:07:09,618 --> 00:07:12,218
He wanted to sail to Croatoan straight away

232
00:07:12,332 --> 00:07:12,602
They rowed back to the ships,

233
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:15,993
ready to sail south

234
00:07:15,723 --> 00:07:15,993
But then a violent storm hit

235
00:07:18,097 --> 00:07:19,537
The ship lost its anchors,

236
00:07:19,537 --> 00:07:21,467
and was nearly wrecked

237
00:07:21,197 --> 00:07:21,467
Ropes snapped,

238
00:07:22,327 --> 00:07:23,768
the sailors were exhausted,

239
00:07:23,768 --> 00:07:26,368
and food and fresh water were running low

240
00:07:26,431 --> 00:07:26,701
They planned to spend the winter in the

241
00:07:28,441 --> 00:07:29,121
Caribbean,

242
00:07:29,121 --> 00:07:31,188
and come back in the spring

243
00:07:30,918 --> 00:07:31,188
But strong winds kept pushing them east,

244
00:07:33,368 --> 00:07:35,128
across the ocean

245
00:07:34,899 --> 00:07:35,169
So the captain decided to turn back to England

246
00:07:38,043 --> 00:07:38,313
John White never returned to America

247
00:07:40,856 --> 00:07:41,126
He later wrote that he could only leave them

248
00:07:43,306 --> 00:07:44,981
in God's hands

249
00:07:44,711 --> 00:07:44,981
He never found out what happened to his

250
00:07:47,001 --> 00:07:47,481
daughter,

251
00:07:47,481 --> 00:07:48,906
or his granddaughter

252
00:07:48,906 --> 00:07:51,506
So what did happen to them?

253
00:07:54,767 --> 00:07:56,464
The simplest theory?

254
00:07:56,464 --> 00:07:58,744
The colonists did exactly what the carving

255
00:07:58,744 --> 00:07:59,290
said

256
00:07:59,290 --> 00:08:01,674
They moved to Croatoan island

257
00:08:01,404 --> 00:08:01,674
Croatoan was Manteo's home,

258
00:08:03,454 --> 00:08:06,054
and his people were friendly to the English

259
00:08:06,084 --> 00:08:06,354
Today,

260
00:08:06,894 --> 00:08:09,231
that island is called Hatteras

261
00:08:08,961 --> 00:08:09,231
It's a long,

262
00:08:09,971 --> 00:08:11,651
thin island in the Outer Banks,

263
00:08:11,651 --> 00:08:14,185
about fifty miles south of Roanoke

264
00:08:13,915 --> 00:08:14,185
Archaeologists digging there have found English

265
00:08:16,645 --> 00:08:17,325
objects,

266
00:08:17,325 --> 00:08:18,845
like part of a sword handle,

267
00:08:18,845 --> 00:08:20,698
and a writing slate

268
00:08:20,428 --> 00:08:20,698
They've also found pieces of guns,

269
00:08:22,558 --> 00:08:24,798
and bits of metal and glass from the right

270
00:08:24,798 --> 00:08:25,728
time

271
00:08:25,458 --> 00:08:25,728
Some experts say these items could have arrived

272
00:08:28,308 --> 00:08:28,788
later,

273
00:08:28,788 --> 00:08:30,164
through trade

274
00:08:29,894 --> 00:08:30,164
Others believe the colonists slowly joined the

275
00:08:32,844 --> 00:08:33,944
Croatoan people,

276
00:08:33,944 --> 00:08:36,336
and became part of their community

277
00:08:36,066 --> 00:08:36,336
And years later,

278
00:08:37,235 --> 00:08:39,595
there were stories of grey-eyed islanders who

279
00:08:39,595 --> 00:08:41,485
could read from books

280
00:08:41,065 --> 00:08:41,485
If that's true,

281
00:08:42,345 --> 00:08:44,516
their descendants may still live in the area

282
00:08:44,516 --> 00:08:45,636
today

283
00:08:49,367 --> 00:08:50,247
But in 2012,

284
00:08:50,247 --> 00:08:51,367
a new clue appeared,

285
00:08:51,367 --> 00:08:53,767
hidden on a map John White himself had drawn,

286
00:08:53,767 --> 00:08:55,917
kept at the British Museum

287
00:08:55,647 --> 00:08:55,917
The map was called La Virginea Pars,

288
00:08:58,017 --> 00:09:00,277
painted by White's own hand

289
00:09:00,007 --> 00:09:00,277
Under a tiny paper patch,

290
00:09:02,017 --> 00:09:03,897
researchers found a hidden symbol:

291
00:09:03,897 --> 00:09:04,377
a fort,

292
00:09:04,377 --> 00:09:06,777
drawn about fifty miles inland

293
00:09:06,592 --> 00:09:06,862
Scientists used light and special scans to see

294
00:09:09,522 --> 00:09:11,071
what lay underneath

295
00:09:10,801 --> 00:09:11,071
Archaeologists dug at that spot...

296
00:09:13,537 --> 00:09:15,577
and found pieces of English pottery from the

297
00:09:15,577 --> 00:09:16,913
right period

298
00:09:16,643 --> 00:09:16,913
The spot was near where two rivers meet,

299
00:09:19,013 --> 00:09:21,613
at the western end of Albemarle Sound

300
00:09:21,559 --> 00:09:21,829
They called it Site X

301
00:09:23,564 --> 00:09:23,834
Some of the pottery was a type made in

302
00:09:25,854 --> 00:09:26,334
England,

303
00:09:26,334 --> 00:09:28,094
called Border ware

304
00:09:27,884 --> 00:09:28,154
So maybe the colonists split up

305
00:09:30,270 --> 00:09:31,190
Some going south,

306
00:09:31,190 --> 00:09:33,270
and others heading inland

307
00:09:32,971 --> 00:09:33,391
But some experts say the pottery could have

308
00:09:35,571 --> 00:09:37,651
come from later settlers

309
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:43,462
And then there are the darker theories

310
00:09:43,462 --> 00:09:45,702
Because not every version of this story has a

311
00:09:45,702 --> 00:09:47,142
happy ending

312
00:09:46,931 --> 00:09:47,201
Scientists studied the rings of very old

313
00:09:49,581 --> 00:09:51,835
cypress trees in the area

314
00:09:51,565 --> 00:09:51,835
And the tree rings revealed something shocking:

315
00:09:54,215 --> 00:09:56,535
the colonists arrived during the worst drought

316
00:09:56,535 --> 00:09:58,404
in eight hundred years

317
00:09:58,134 --> 00:09:58,404
Even the local people struggled to find enough

318
00:10:00,824 --> 00:10:01,797
food

319
00:10:01,527 --> 00:10:01,797
Without crops,

320
00:10:02,697 --> 00:10:05,017
starvation and disease may have taken many of

321
00:10:05,017 --> 00:10:06,452
the colonists

322
00:10:06,182 --> 00:10:06,452
When the English founded Jamestown in 1607,

323
00:10:09,592 --> 00:10:12,192
they heard rumors about the lost colonists

324
00:10:12,374 --> 00:10:12,644
Some think they were attacked,

325
00:10:14,144 --> 00:10:15,784
perhaps by Spanish soldiers,

326
00:10:15,784 --> 00:10:18,041
or by enemies on the mainland

327
00:10:17,771 --> 00:10:18,041
One report claimed some of them had been living

328
00:10:20,381 --> 00:10:22,141
with another people further north,

329
00:10:22,141 --> 00:10:24,123
and were later attacked

330
00:10:23,853 --> 00:10:24,123
And some famous clues,

331
00:10:25,423 --> 00:10:28,023
like carved stones found in the 1930s,

332
00:10:28,023 --> 00:10:30,493
are now believed to be fakes

333
00:10:30,073 --> 00:10:30,493
Dozens of these stones turned up,

334
00:10:32,313 --> 00:10:34,473
telling a story that seemed too good to be

335
00:10:34,473 --> 00:10:35,593
true

336
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:40,961
So where does that leave us?

337
00:10:40,961 --> 00:10:42,801
More than four hundred years later,

338
00:10:42,801 --> 00:10:45,201
the mystery is still unsolved

339
00:10:44,976 --> 00:10:45,246
Roanoke Island is now home to the Fort Raleigh

340
00:10:48,146 --> 00:10:49,906
National Historic Site

341
00:10:49,775 --> 00:10:50,045
Every year,

342
00:10:50,705 --> 00:10:52,025
archaeologists dig,

343
00:10:52,025 --> 00:10:53,889
looking for new clues

344
00:10:53,619 --> 00:10:53,889
Almost every summer since 1937,

345
00:10:56,469 --> 00:10:59,149
a play about the Lost Colony has been performed

346
00:10:59,149 --> 00:11:00,488
on the island

347
00:11:00,218 --> 00:11:00,488
Some hope that DNA could one day connect

348
00:11:03,108 --> 00:11:05,708
families living today to the lost colonists

349
00:11:06,035 --> 00:11:06,305
The nearby town is named Manteo,

350
00:11:08,445 --> 00:11:10,845
after the colonists' loyal friend

351
00:11:10,653 --> 00:11:10,923
Until then,

352
00:11:11,623 --> 00:11:13,823
nobody knows for sure what happened to the

353
00:11:13,823 --> 00:11:15,441
people of Roanoke

354
00:11:15,171 --> 00:11:15,441
And the county is named Dare,

355
00:11:17,101 --> 00:11:19,525
after the little girl who vanished

356
00:11:19,255 --> 00:11:19,525
Virginia Dare

357
00:11:20,956 --> 00:11:23,556
The first English child born in America

358
00:11:23,551 --> 00:11:24,021
Maybe one day,

359
00:11:24,921 --> 00:11:26,401
the next clue will turn up,

360
00:11:26,401 --> 00:11:27,161
in the ground,

361
00:11:27,161 --> 00:11:29,241
or in our DNA

362
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:32,056
One hundred and fifteen people

363
00:11:32,056 --> 00:11:33,499
One carved word

364
00:11:33,499 --> 00:11:34,742
No answer

365
00:11:34,692 --> 00:11:34,742
Was it Croatoan?

366
00:11:36,559 --> 00:11:38,011
A hidden fort?

367
00:11:38,011 --> 00:11:39,771
Or something darker?

368
00:11:39,677 --> 00:11:39,777
What do you think happened to the Lost Colony?

369
00:11:42,223 --> 00:11:42,273
Tell me in the comments

370
00:11:43,910 --> 00:11:43,960
And subscribe,

371
00:11:44,860 --> 00:11:47,460
so you don't miss the next mystery
